From: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 13:23:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] x86/pci: skip INTx fallback entirely on PS4 to prevent IRQ
 storms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------false"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------false
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit


 The PS4 Southbridge (Aeolia) supports MSI for all onboard devices. When
 devices fall back to legacy INTx routing (which isn't wired up correctly
 in the BIOS/ACPI tables), they share IRQ 0 or an unmapped IRQ line,
 resulting in severe interrupt storms and lost interrupts under load.
 Skip legacy fallback completely on PS4.
---
 arch/x86/pci/irq.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)


--------------false
Content-Type: text/x-patch; name="0105-x86-pci-skip-INTx-fallback-entirely-on-PS4-to-preven.patch"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="0105-x86-pci-skip-INTx-fallback-entirely-on-PS4-to-preven.patch"

diff --git a/arch/x86/pci/irq.c b/arch/x86/pci/irq.c
index 0de436316a1dd147c057ac6b2db56701e357834f..2aee854129831883a342b9f4efda0e75901ee1df 100644
--- a/arch/x86/pci/irq.c
+++ b/arch/x86/pci/irq.c
@@ -1720,6 +1720,11 @@ static int pirq_enable_irq(struct pci_dev *dev)
 {
 	u8 pin = 0;
 
+	if (!boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_HYPERVISOR) && boot_cpu_data.x86_vendor == X86_VENDOR_AMD && boot_cpu_data.x86 == 0x16) {
+		/* On PS4, skip INTx fallback entirely to prevent IRQ storms */
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	pci_read_config_byte(dev, PCI_INTERRUPT_PIN, &pin);
 	if (pin && !pcibios_lookup_irq(dev, 1)) {
 		char *msg = "";

--------------false--


